      "problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to $16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Both the first and the second logarithmic terms have a base of $e$ and an argument of $8.$ Therefore, we can combine them by adding their coefficients.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16) & =(16-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16) \\\\  & =15\\operatorname{ln}⁡(8)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(16)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
